      "confidence": 0.95,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 34,
      "line_end": 35,
      "title": "Search query built from request input",
      "description": "Search pastes the name query parameter into the SQL text with fmt.Sprintf. A quote in name breaks out of the string literal. Any caller of GET /users can run arbitrary SQL against the database. That caller can read or change every table. Pass name to QueryContext as a bound parameter. Keep the SQL text constant.",
      "suggested_change": "\trows, err := h.DB.QueryContext(r.Context(), \"SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE name = ?\", name)",
      "source": "semgrep:go.lang.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Search pastes the name query parameter into the SQL text with fmt.Sprintf. A quote in name breaks out of the string literal.",
      "consequence": "Any caller of GET /users can run arbitrary SQL against the database. That caller can read or change every table.",
      "fix": "Pass name to QueryContext as a bound parameter. Keep the SQL text constant."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 63,
      "line_end": 63,
      "title": "Mutex left locked on missing key",
      "description": "Count takes h.mu before it checks the key. The empty-key branch returns without unlocking h.mu. One request to GET /count without a key leaves h.mu locked forever. Every later Count request then blocks, and its goroutine leaks. Check the key before taking the lock. Alternatively, unlock with defer right after Lock.",
      "suggested_change": null,
      "source": "semgrep:trailofbits.go.missing-unlock-before-return.missing-unlock-before-return",
      "candidate": "c2",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Count takes h.mu before it checks the key. The empty-key branch returns without unlocking h.mu.",
      "consequence": "One request to GET /count without a key leaves h.mu locked forever. Every later Count request then blocks, and its goroutine leaks.",
      "fix": "Check the key before taking the lock. Alternatively, unlock with defer right after Lock."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 83,
      "line_end": 83,
      "title": "Response body closed before error check",
      "description": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close() before it checks err. When http.Get fails, resp is nil and the deferred call dereferences nil. Each request to GET /upstream panics while the upstream is unreachable. The client gets a dropped connection instead of the intended 502. Move the defer below the error check.",
      "suggested_change": "\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\tdefer resp.Body.Close()",
      "source": null,
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close() before it checks err. When http.Get fails, resp is nil and the deferred call dereferences nil.",
      "consequence": "Each request to GET /upstream panics while the upstream is unreachable. The client gets a dropped connection instead of the intended 502.",
      "fix": "Move the defer below the error check."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "maintainability",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 31,
      "line_end": 88,
      "title": "New handlers have no covering test",
      "description": "This change adds Search, Count, Upstream and fetchStatus. The repository has no test file that exercises them. Tests would have caught the lock leak and the nil body panic. Future changes to these handlers can regress without notice. Add httptest-based tests for each handler. Include the empty-key and unreachable-upstream paths.",
